{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he blessed them on that day, saying, etc.</b> The meaning is: he blessed them with so many blessings, to the point that there is no blessing above it, until all say of you it is fitting to bless Israel." "And its saying <b>and he set Efraim</b> etc. — the meaning is: by means of this expression he fixed a place of precedence for the younger before Menasheh, for who among the children of Israel would change the established practice of Yaakov our father and say to his son, ״May Elohim set you as Menasheh and as Efraim״? And this statement served as a sign that Efraim precedes Menasheh in everything."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:11.649243143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}